# Cross-frame Bounds on a RESOURCE element array (error-model.md §11, Increment
# 2.1d): a deep OOB on a `Vector[String]` propagates the Bounds fault; the
# callee's declared return is the OWNED element (String), so the return-boundary
# materialization clones the borrow — no Ptr(T) leak. Run under ASan/UBSan: clean.
String getname(Vector[String] names, int i): names[i]

void main():
    Vector[String] names = ["alice", "bob"]
    String a = getname(names, 99) catch Fault.Bounds: "missing"
    print(a)                                 # missing (OOB caught)
    String b = getname(names, 1) catch Fault.Bounds: "missing"
    print(b)                                 # bob (in-bounds)
